    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-nov-guts-2017-p5.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Answer: 6\nWe have \\(a_{2}=2, a_{3}=3, a_{4}=7, a_{5}=7!+1=5041\\), and \\(a_{6}=5041!+1\\). But\n\n\\[5041!+1 \\gg 5041 \\cdot 5040 \\cdot 5039>10^{10}\\]\n\nHence, the answer is 6 .",
